# Orchestration server (Goblin Cannon)

The local dashboard + API live under `orchestration/` (Fastify + Vite). **Source edits are in `orchestration/src/` and `orchestration/client/`; Node runs compiled output from `orchestration/dist/`.**

## When to rebuild

After **any** change to orchestration **TypeScript** (`orchestration/src/**/*.ts`) or **client** (`orchestration/client/**`), run a full build **before** testing in the browser or restarting the server:

```powershell
Set-Location "c:\Users\josep\Desktop\Coding Projects\goblin-cannon\orchestration"; npm run build
```

If you only changed **config JSON** (`orchestration.config.local.json`) or **prompts** under `orchestration/prompts/`, a rebuild is **not** required unless those files are bundled at build time (prompts are read at runtime from the package — no rebuild). Still restart the Node process so `loadConfig()` cache resets if config changed.

If the Cursor **agent** returns no stdout/stderr on Windows, the planner uses **`plannerFallback`** (default true) to create one task from the problem text so the pipeline can run. Env: `ORCH_PLANNER_FALLBACK=0` to disable.

After execution, **`requireExecutionGitChanges`** (default true) fails the pipeline if the worktree has no new commits and no dirty files — catches silent no-ops when the CLI exits 0 without editing. Env: `ORCH_REQUIRE_EXEC_GIT_CHANGES=0` to disable (e.g. debugging).

After Godot tests pass, **`autoMergeOnPass`** (default true) merges the task branch into `main`/`master` in the main repo, removes the worktree, and frees the capacity slot. Set **`autoMergeOnPass`: false** in config to keep branches for manual merge. Failed tests or merge conflicts leave the task failed and release the slot (worktree may remain until you remove it via the API).

**`limits.maxParallelWorktrees`** (default **4** in `orchestration.config.example.json`) controls how many agent worktrees may run at once; completed tasks release slots automatically.

If logs show **empty planner stdout**, **`Warning: 'print'… Electron`**, **no git changes**, or a stray **`agent`** tab, **`cursor.cmd`** is often forwarding flags to Electron. Prefer the standalone **`agent`** binary (see **`orchestration/README.md`** Headless agent): env **`CURSOR_AGENT_BIN`**, or a **full path** to **`agent.cmd`/`agent.exe`** in **`cursorCli.command`** (that path wins over user **`CURSOR_CLI`**), or rely on **`%LOCALAPPDATA%\cursor-agent\agent.cmd`** before `where cursor`. Plus **`CURSOR_API_KEY`** in **`cursorCli.env`** or the process environment.

## Restart the server

1. Find the listener on **8787** (`netstat -ano | findstr ":8787"`), then `taskkill /PID <pid> /F`.
2. From `orchestration/`: `npm start` (serves `http://127.0.0.1:8787`).

Godot path for tests: see `godot-path.mdc` and `orchestration/orchestration.config.local.json`.
